# Copy to frontend/.env (gitignored). Bun auto-loads frontend/.env from this
# directory, so both `bun run dev` and `bunx vitest run` pick it up.

# --- Local dev server (bun run dev) ---
# Points the app at the local docker Postgres (docker-compose.yml, port 5435).
# On the production VPS the systemd unit supplies DATABASE_URL instead
# (/etc/market-pulse.env), so this is dev-only.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5435/market_pulse

# --- DB-integration test suite (src/server/db/*.test.ts) ---
# These suites open a real Postgres and mutate tables, so they run ONLY against
# an isolated throwaway DB — never DATABASE_URL. This repo is developed on the
# prod VPS, so without TEST_DATABASE_URL the suites SKIP (see db-test-guard.ts)
# and vitest's connection is routed to an unroutable sentinel, never prod.
#
# To run them, create and migrate a throwaway DB, then set TEST_DATABASE_URL:
#   createdb -h localhost -p 5435 -U postgres market_pulse_test
#   DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:PW@localhost:5435/market_pulse_test \
#     bun run src/server/db/migrate.ts
# TEST_DATABASE_URL must differ from DATABASE_URL (a match is treated as prod).
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5435/market_pulse_test
